# Immediate input, minimal Bluetooth

When changing DualSense input sampling, nav, or HID I/O in this repo:

## Prefer immediate reads

1. Prefer an immediate input read over saving CPU or timer wakes. Do **not** insert a poll sleep to be polite to the system.
2. Do **not** busy-spin: block in the HID read so the thread wakes when the next report arrives (`read_timeout(0)` to drain, then a short block ≈ one wired report interval when empty).
3. While pad input is live (start screen, reopen gesture, Pad Input), keep the UI snapshot apply cadence in the same ballpark as the pad report rate (about 4ms wired).

## Keep Bluetooth traffic low

4. Reading reports the pad is already sending does **not** count as extra Bluetooth traffic.
5. Do **not** add output reports, feature reports, or handle open/close churn in order to read faster.
6. Lightbar, battery poll, and Identify stay as infrequent as they are now. The one-time Bluetooth full-report (calibration) request stays one-time.
7. On a short read timeout, keep the open handle and last reading. Drop the handle only on a real I/O error — reconnecting adds Bluetooth setup traffic and drops in-progress presses.

## Diagnostics

8. This does **not** relax [debug-diagnostics.mdc](debug-diagnostics.mdc). Release builds stay quiet; gate investigation-volume traces with debug helpers.
